{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1357904-what-can-quantum-9-novas-make","id":1357904,"title":"What can Quantum 9 novas make?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-30T17:13:20-08:00","id":1357904,"title":"What can Quantum 9 novas make?","content":"Okay, the answer for quantum 10 novas is &quot;anything they want but largely they're off to other universes.&quot; <br /> <br /> But what could quantum 9 novas make? I'm asking because what would be the limits of the kind of weirdness you might find in the Aeon trinity era as you explore. The players guide had some tremendous powers before quantum 10, but I'm not certain if the designers intend to go that route again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's start with some possible examples to see if thse sound like what a nova with 9 quantum and a boat load of powers could do:<br /> <br /> 1. A robotic terraforming engine that has been warping to planets and remaking them in earth's image (even ods on whether or not it cares if people already exist).<br /> <br /> 2. A fleet of war machines, preparing for the attack on earth--but silent. (the nova hit quantum 10 and lost interest). <br /> <br /> 3. A vast museum, full of the nova's exploits and the true story of the nova age, with lovingly crafted exhibits--and perhaps a few secrets unknown on earth. <br /> It also comes with a guide who is quite capable of protecting his charge.<br /> <br /> 4. A particularly quircky nova found a way to duplicate human memories, and took copies of humanity from earth. They (or their descendants) believe they were kidnapped from earth. Bonus points if the settlement is &quot;new&quot; so these are actually people out of time, dating from before the ultimatum. <br /> <br /> 5. A gigantic hard-tech warp gate that can send ships to a far off galaxy--but with no idea what is on the other end...<br /> <br /> Anything 